# This is a list of commands that can be sent to the spacecraft
# args are 16 bit except the special code 99099099 which is replaced with the unix time
LIST, namespaces, None, Operations, SSTV, File System
LIST, FOLDER, sstv_queue 1, sstv_queue 2, sstv_queue 3, bin, lib, config, PACSAT dir, upload, whole orbit data
LIST, ENABLE, false, true
LIST, OVERWRITE, false, true
LIST, UPLINK MODE, Off, All stations, Command Stations Only
LIST, FILE_MODE, use id for file name, user file name
# Name, Name space, cmd, arg0, arg1, arg2, arg3, argName0, argName1, argName2, argName3, confirm, use reset/uptime, description
Set X Band Rpt Mode,1,2,0,0,0,0,Enable,NONE,NONE,NONE,false,false,Set cross band repeater mode
SSTV Send,2,3,0,120,0,0,Folder,Cooldown(s),NONE,NONE,false,false,Set SSTV mode
SSTV Loop,2,4,0,120,4,0,Folder,Cooldown(s),Period(h),NONE,false,false,Set SSTV loop send mode
SSTV Stop,2,5,0,0,0,0,NONE,NONE,NONE,NONE,false,false,Stop SSTV mode
APRS Mode,1,6,0,0,0,0,Enable,NONE,NONE,NONE,false,false,Set APRS mode
File System Mode,1,7,0,0,0,0,Enable,NONE,NONE,NONE,false,false,Set PACSAT mode
Set Time,1,9,99099099,0,0,0,UnixTime,NONE,NONE,NONE,true,false,Set the time on the spacecraft
Pacsat Broadcast,3,1,0,0,0,0,Enable,Period,Timeout,NONE,false,false,Pacsat Broadcasts <enable> <period> <timeout>
File Uploads,3,2,0,0,0,0,Uplink Mode,Period,Timeout,NONE,false,false,Enable or disable File Uploads <enable> <period> <timeout>
Install File,3,3,0,0,0,0,FileId,NONE,Folder,Overwrite,false,false,Copy a file from the PACSAT Directory to a folder and give it a 4 byte hex name that matches the id.  Can be removed later with a command. Params <file-id> <folder> <force>
Install User File,3,4,0,0,0,0,FileId,NONE,Folder,Overwrite,false,false,Copy a file from the PACSAT Directory to a folder and give it the user file name.  Required to install scripts or binaries that must be found in the path. May also be useful to order files alphabetically.  Can't then delete a single file with a command but can later purge an entire foder. Params <file-id> <folder> <force>
Delete File,3,5,0,0,0,0,FileId,NONE,Folder,NONE,true,false,Delete a file on the ARISS-PI. Typically this leaves the original copy in the PACSAT dir.  To delete the original copy specify the PACSAT Dir folder
Delete Folder Contents,3,6,0,0,0,0,Folder,NONE,Folder,NONE,true,false,Uploads <4 byte file-id> <folder> <force>
PM1 (School Contact),1,1,0,0,0,0,NONE,NONE,NONE,NONE,true,false,Set PM1 (school contact) and will stop listening for ground commands
